# The partner repositories molrec is checked against, resolved by
# molcrafts-ci's shared resolver (molcrafts_ci.partners) at the CI_REF commit:
# for the workflows (actions/setup-partners) and, through scripts/partners.py,
# for the git hooks (`partners.py check` / `run`) alike. A local push is judged
# against the same molrs commit as CI, never against whatever ../molrs happens
# to have checked out.
#
# KEY=VALUE lines only. SELF is this repository's directory in CI's sibling
# layout. CI_REF is the full molcrafts-ci commit: scripts/partners.py runs the
# resolver at it, and every `uses: MolCrafts/molcrafts-ci/actions/...@` in
# .github/workflows names the same commit (`partners.py check` fails
# otherwise).
#
# MOLRS_REF is used exactly as written -- a branch, tag or full commit; no
# same-named-branch matching and no sibling fallback. On dev it is `dev`. A
# change spanning molrec and molrs pins the partner's commit here explicitly
# until that lands (see "Partners" in CLAUDE.md); a release names a tag or
# commit.
#
# uv.lock records molrs's package metadata (its version and dependencies), not
# a commit. When the resolved molrs changes that metadata, `uv lock --check`
# fails; relock in a commit of its own:
#   scripts/partners.py run -- sh -c 'uv lock && cp uv.lock "$PARTNERS_SOURCE/"'
SELF=molrec
CI_REF=03352583738d9424ce37996ef9e04df9290087ba
MOLRS_REPOSITORY=MolCrafts/molrs
# Pinned while molrs's refactor/atomic-number-species (MolCrafts/molrs#143)
# lands; back to dev once it is merged.
MOLRS_REF=e6bf78e20855a07719fca0a6a99436dad56bc4f8
